      "writtenOn": "2019-08-05T21:29:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Only the stop sequence would reset the bus, not the start sequence.\nIf the fsm is stuck in a certain state (even one that isn\u0027t pulling sda low), the next transaction could leave the i2cs into a stuck at 0 state, preventing the stop condition from being seen by the i2cs block and wedging the bus.\nInstead of setting timers/interrupts to detect when the bus is hung, I though it would be easier just to apply the workaround to reset the i2cs fsm every time the tpm reset is detected.",
      "parentUuid": "90210b1b_a87ecf4e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 109,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 110,
        "endChar": 9
